    {
      "@id": "reaction:Amidation_BenzoicAcid_Ethylamine",
      "@type": [
        "cpo:StoichiometricReaction",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Amidation of benzoic acid with ethylamine",
      "schema:description": "Benzoic acid + Ethylamine + HATU + Diisopropylamine > N-Ethylbenzamide + HOAt + Tetramethylurea + Diisopropylammonium + Hexafluorophosphate",
      "schema:comment": "Net balance of the amidation in the AI4Green record AI4-001. From the ELN: the reaction SMILES OC(=O)C1=CC=CC=C1.CCN>>CCNC(=O)C1=CC=CC=C1 (benzoic acid + ethylamine > N-ethylbenzamide) and the reagents HATU and diisopropylamine. Added by curation (suggested by Claude Code, confirmed by Laura Fadler on 29.09.2026): the coefficients of the reagents and the by-products HOAt, tetramethylurea and diisopropylammonium hexafluorophosphate (as its two ions), which the ELN leaves out (E. Valeur and M. Bradley, Amide bond formation: beyond the myth of coupling reagents, Chem. Soc. Rev. 2009, 38, 606-631, doi:10.1039/B701677H). A net balance, not a mechanism. The ELN draws HATU as the O-uronium isomer; the balance is the same for the N-isomer. The ELN names the base diisopropylamine; diisopropylethylamine (DIPEA) is the usual one - taken over as written. The solvent DMF of the record is no participant: a solvent is stated at the phase it is the medium of (cpo:hasSolvent; decided by Laura Fadler on 01.10.2026). No RInChI yet: it is only generated by the RInChI software of the InChI Trust.",
      "cpo:hasParticipant": [
        {
          "@id": "reaction:Amidation_BenzoicAcid_Ethylamine_Participant_BenzoicAcid"
        },
