    {
      "@id": "reaction:RCF_SpruceWood",
      "@type": [
        "cpo:LumpedReaction",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Reductive catalytic fractionation of spruce wood",
      "schema:description": "Lignin (of spruce wood, dissolved in methanol) + H2 (Pd/C) > lignin oil (mainly 4-propylguaiacol); the cellulose stays behind as pulp",
      "schema:comment": "The reaction of the Chemotion records LCJ-R5 and LCJ-R8 ('Reductive Catalytic Fractionation (RCF) of spruce wood pellets'; reaction class 'biomass_fractionation' in the segment 'Reaction Details'). A lumped reaction: lignin and lignin oil are no single species, so there is no balanced equation and no stoichiometric coefficient. In the 'lignin-first' picture the lignin of the wood dissolves and is broken down at the catalyst; the cellulose pulp the records list as a second product is what stays behind, not a product of the reaction. Participants and roles written by curation (suggested by Claude Code, confirmed by Laura Fadler on 05.10.2026 for the Chemotion example). No RInChI: the one of the records is empty (no structures).",
      "cpo:hasParticipant": [
        {
          "@id": "reaction:RCF_SpruceWood_Participant_Lignin"
        },
        {
          "@id": "reaction:RCF_SpruceWood_Participant_Hydrogen"
        },
        {
          "@id": "reaction:RCF_SpruceWood_Participant_Palladium"
        },
        {
          "@id": "reaction:RCF_SpruceWood_Participant_ActivatedCarbon"
        },
        {
          "@id": "reaction:RCF_SpruceWood_Participant_Propylguaiacol"
        }
      ],
      "schema:subjectOf": [
        {
          "@id": "reaction:Record_Chemotion_LCJ-R5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "reaction:Record_Chemotion_LCJ-R8"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "reaction:RCF_SpruceWood_Participant_Lignin",
      "@type": [
        "cpo:ReactionParticipant",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "dcterms:hasPart": {
        "@id": "chem:Lignin"
      },
      "cpo:hasChemicalRole": {
        "@id": "cpo:Substrate"
      },
      "cpo:participatesIn": {
        "@id": "reaction:RCF_SpruceWood"
      },
      "schema:comment": "Not named in the ELN as a substance: the lignin of the starting material (Chemotion LCJ-R5, LCJ-R8: spruce wood), which the records' products come from ('lignin-derived liquid product', 'G-unit depolymerisation'). Role Substrate by curation: its skeleton ends up in the phenolic products (suggested by Claude Code, confirmed by Laura Fadler on 05.10.2026 for the Chemotion example)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "reaction:RCF_SpruceWood_Participant_Hydrogen",
