      "schema:comment": "TEMPLATE of the co-precipitation of a Prussian blue analogue from the ferricyanide ion and 5 metal(II) ions in equal amounts in water, net-ionic: potassium and chloride stay in solution as spectator ions. The metal ions and the product are placeholders; the fixed reactions of the concrete metals specialize the template (hlo:specializationOf; made with generator/workflow/library_prerun/pba_reactions.py), and a sheet names those. Idealized composition: no potassium, water or vacancies in the lattice, the metals equimolar - the real composition of the precipitate is only known after its characterization (Laura Fadler, 05.10.2026). A net balance, not a mechanism. Added by curation for the series pba_synthesis (suggested by Claude Code, decided by Laura Fadler and Meng Kong on 06.10.2026 for the series pba_synthesis); replaces the template of the same ID from the salts (05.10.2026, kept in projects/pba_synthesis/curation/archive/).",
